IMPORT prelude

-- Death Penalty Abolition Act 1973 (Cth) — THE NOUNS. No rules here.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00004.txt (compilation of
-- 19 April 2010). Seat: the person charged with an offence.

§ `Nouns`

-- s 3(2)-(3): the law under which the offence arises.
DECLARE `Kind of law` IS ONE OF
    `a law of the Commonwealth`
    `a law of a Territory`
    -- s 3(2): "to the extent to which the powers of the Parliament permit"
    `an Imperial Act within the Parliament's powers`
    `a law of a State`
    `some other law`

DECLARE `Offence` HAS
    `the law`                                           IS A `Kind of law`
    -- s 5: the law provides that a person is liable to the punishment of
    -- death.
    `the law provides for death`                        IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Penalty in place of death` IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment for life`

DECLARE `Death penalty position` HAS
    `the Act applies`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `death may be imposed`                              IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the penalty in place of death`                     IS A MAYBE `Penalty in place of death`
